WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.151
Team performance depends on shared mental models.

00:00:03.151 --> 00:00:10.160
People need a common understanding of goals, roles, constraints, current status, risks, and expected actions.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:15.241
Without that shared picture, individuals may work hard in different directions.

00:00:15.241 --> 00:00:21.736
Communication is not just information exchange; it is how a team keeps its operating picture aligned.

00:00:21.736 --> 00:00:25.787
Clear handoffs and defined responsibilities reduce hidden work.

00:00:25.787 --> 00:00:34.918
A good handoff explains what changed, what remains unresolved, what decisions were made, what risks exist, and what the next person should do.

00:00:34.918 --> 00:00:42.185
Documentation supports continuity when people are absent, tired, new to the work, or operating across time zones.

00:00:42.185 --> 00:00:45.465
Work that exists only in someone's head is fragile.

00:00:45.465 --> 00:00:55.947
Psychological safety at a practical level means people can raise concerns, admit uncertainty, ask for help, and report mistakes without being punished for honesty.

00:00:55.947 --> 00:00:58.262
It does not mean avoiding standards.

00:00:58.262 --> 00:01:02.249
It means the team can surface reality early enough to respond.

00:01:02.249 --> 00:01:07.779
High-performing teams make it safe to tell the truth and expected to improve the work.

00:01:07.779 --> 00:01:12.087
Meeting hygiene, escalation paths, and feedback culture all matter.

00:01:12.087 --> 00:01:15.560
Meetings should have purpose, ownership, and outcomes.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.711
Escalation paths should be clear before a crisis.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:22.441
Feedback should be specific, timely, and tied to behavior.

00:01:22.441 --> 00:01:30.736
The goal is to make team performance less dependent on heroic individuals and more dependent on visible, repeatable coordination.

00:01:30.736 --> 00:01:33.116
Healthy teams also make work visible.

00:01:33.116 --> 00:01:38.324
Hidden assumptions, hidden blockers, and hidden overload create performance risk.

00:01:38.324 --> 00:01:44.176
Shared boards, written decisions, concise updates, and explicit ownership reduce ambiguity.

00:01:44.176 --> 00:01:51.893
When the team can see the work, it can rebalance priorities before individuals have to compensate through heroic effort.
